{icon:"🏛️",title:"UNESCO World Heritage Sites in India",text:"India has numerous UNESCO World Heritage Sites, recognised for outstanding cultural or natural significance.",example:"The Taj Mahal is one of India's most famous World Heritage Sites.",dyk:"India has one of the highest numbers of UNESCO sites in the world.",real:"Visiting or learning about these sites connects you to significant landmarks."},
{icon:"🎉",title:"Important National Symbols and Days",text:"India has various national symbols and observes important days commemorating historical events.",example:"Independence Day, 15th August, and Republic Day, 26th January, are key observances.",dyk:"National symbols like the flag carry deep historical significance.",real:"Participating in school celebrations for these days connects you to India's identity."}
