{icon:"🏏",title:"Cricket in India",text:"Cricket is one of the most popular sports in India, played and followed by millions.",example:"A cricket team has 11 players.",dyk:"India has won the Cricket World Cup multiple times.",real:"Watching or playing a cricket match with friends shows this sport's popularity in India."},
{icon:"⚽",title:"Popular Sports Around the World",text:"Different sports are popular in different countries, like football, basketball and hockey.",example:"Football is the most popular sport in many countries worldwide.",dyk:"The Olympics bring together athletes from many sports and countries every four years.",real:"Watching international sporting events shows the popularity of global sports."},
{icon:"🏑",title:"Hockey: India's Traditional Sport",text:"Hockey has a rich history in India, with the country winning multiple Olympic gold medals in the past.",example:"Major Dhyan Chand is a legendary Indian hockey player.",dyk:"India dominated Olympic hockey for decades in the early-to-mid 20th century.",real:"Learning about hockey legends like Dhyan Chand connects you to India's sporting history."},
{icon:"🏅",title:"The Olympics",text:"The Olympics is a major international sporting event held every four years, featuring many different sports.",example:"Athletes from around the world compete in the Olympics.",dyk:"The Olympics were first held in ancient Greece, over 2,000 years ago.",real:"Watching Olympic events on TV shows athletes competing in a wide range of sports."},
{icon:"🏃",title:"Famous Indian Athletes",text:"India has produced many famous athletes who have achieved success in various sports.",example:"P.T. Usha is a famous Indian athlete known for sprinting.",dyk:"Milkha Singh, known as the 'Flying Sikh', is a legendary Indian sprinter.",real:"Learning about famous Indian athletes inspires young people to pursue sports."}
